      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1742920244785,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Functional Requirements: \n\n1. streaming server already there. \n2. live comments -> many people will be connected to streaming -> commenting on system. \n3. other people would be able to see the all comments particular to stream. \n\n\nOut of scope: \n1. we'll not go much in to streaming part only\n   comments and sharing comments to other folks\n\nNon functional Requirements: \n1.  real time processing. \n2. accurate -> comment shouldn't  as much as possible. \n3. comment seeing by other few second is ok, but good availability\n4. scalability. \n5. comment durability -> only at time of streaming  -> persist\n                                                            \n                                                    CAP -> imp -> in nfr.\n                                                          durability always there -> can also skip\nEstimations:  -> ask about scale , don't much go in calculation -> later on. -> save time. -> quick chat with int. \n                     to do calculation later on -> if interviewer say -> then you can do now. \n1.  rough QPS of comments \n2. 1M active user per day.\n3. 1000 comments per second. \n4. concurrent video -> 1M. \n5. total comments per second -> ~1B\n6. Storage -> 100b * 1B -> \n\n\nFeedback -> good idea to write entity before api design -> livecomment , stream ,user,  etc. \n\nApi Designs:  -> don't pass userId -> that usually happen in token, like in header going to be header\nthat will have token and have userId there. \n\n\n1. for comment  ( websocket )\nPOST  -> api/v1/comment/\nRequest: \n{\n   userId: \"\",\n   comments: \"\",\n   streamId: \"\",\n\n}\n\nResponse: \n{\n   statusCode: \n}\n\n1. Read api ->  ( websocket  vs long pooling. )\n\nmessages in batch for optimizating for 5 second; \n\nGET -> api/v1/comments?streamId=\"\"&&from=\"\"&&size=25 , paginated type of api\n\nResponse : \n\n{\n  statusCode: \"\"\n  from: \"\"\n  size: \"\"\n  hits:  [\n     {\n         comment: \"\"\n         author name: \"\"\n         timestampe: \"\"\n         ....\n     },\n     .....\n  ]\n\n}\n\n\nAdding -> reverse -> can have direction sort of thing\n            cursor mechanism than page size -> is good \n\nshare all information explicitly or imlic\n\n\n\nDesign Schema: \n\n\n\n\n\n\nHigh Level Design:\n      \n",
      "fontSize": 20.295408433912346,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Functional Requirements: \n\n1. streaming server already there. \n2. live comments -> many people will be connected to streaming -> commenting on system. \n3. other people would be able to see the all comments particular to stream. \n\n\nOut of scope: \n1. we'll not go much in to streaming part only\n   comments and sharing comments to other folks\n\nNon functional Requirements: \n1.  real time processing. \n2. accurate -> comment shouldn't  as much as possible. \n3. comment seeing by other few second is ok, but good availability\n4. scalability. \n5. comment durability -> only at time of streaming  -> persist\n                                                            \n                                                    CAP -> imp -> in nfr.\n                                                          durability always there -> can also skip\nEstimations:  -> ask about scale , don't much go in calculation -> later on. -> save time. -> quick chat with int. \n                     to do calculation later on -> if interviewer say -> then you can do now. \n1.  rough QPS of comments \n2. 1M active user per day.\n3. 1000 comments per second. \n4. concurrent video -> 1M. \n5. total comments per second -> ~1B\n6. Storage -> 100b * 1B -> \n\n\nFeedback -> good idea to write entity before api design -> livecomment , stream ,user,  etc. \n\nApi Designs:  -> don't pass userId -> that usually happen in token, like in header going to be header\nthat will have token and have userId there. \n\n\n1. for comment  ( websocket )\nPOST  -> api/v1/comment/\nRequest: \n{\n   userId: \"\",\n   comments: \"\",\n   streamId: \"\",\n\n}\n\nResponse: \n{\n   statusCode: \n}\n\n1. Read api ->  ( websocket  vs long pooling. )\n\nmessages in batch for optimizating for 5 second; \n\nGET -> api/v1/comments?streamId=\"\"&&from=\"\"&&size=25 , paginated type of api\n\nResponse : \n\n{\n  statusCode: \"\"\n  from: \"\"\n  size: \"\"\n  hits:  [\n     {\n         comment: \"\"\n         author name: \"\"\n         timestampe: \"\"\n         ....\n     },\n     .....\n  ]\n\n}\n\n\nAdding -> reverse -> can have direction sort of thing\n            cursor mechanism than page size -> is good \n\nshare all information explicitly or imlic\n\n\n\nDesign Schema: \n\n\n\n\n\n\nHigh Level Design:\n      \n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
